From 1a3cd3a8dc9af939f2dc26f8142ecf538b6cdd1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:09:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/22] thingino-onvif: emit each zoom default space in schema
 order

Out of xs:sequence order, zeep (Frigate's ONVIF parser) dropped the pan/tilt
spaces, so Frigate showed zoom buttons but no arrows.
---
 ...h-zoom-default-space-in-schema-order.patch | 402 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 402 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package/thingino-onvif/0001-ptz-emit-each-zoom-default-space-in-schema-order.patch

diff --git a/package/thingino-onvif/0001-ptz-emit-each-zoom-default-space-in-schema-order.patch b/package/thingino-onvif/0001-ptz-emit-each-zoom-default-space-in-schema-order.patch
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..e2ec6997c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/thingino-onvif/0001-ptz-emit-each-zoom-default-space-in-schema-order.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,402 @@
+From 52879ed480d9856c05b452f177b07ceccaff053f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:19:16 -0400
+Subject: [PATCH] ptz: emit each zoom default space in schema order
+
+ZOOM_DEFAULT_SPACES put all three zoom defaults right after
+DefaultAbsolutePantTiltPositionSpace. PTZConfiguration is an
+xs:sequence -- absolute pan/tilt, absolute zoom, relative pan/tilt,
+relative zoom, continuous pan/tilt, continuous zoom -- so with zoom
+enabled the relative and continuous zoom spaces came before their
+pan/tilt counterparts. zeep, which Frigate parses ONVIF with, drops
+elements that arrive out of order: it read the zoom spaces and lost
+DefaultRelativePanTiltTranslationSpace and
+DefaultContinuousPanTiltVelocitySpace, so Frigate showed zoom buttons
+and no pan/tilt controls. Cameras without zoom were unaffected, the
+placeholder expanding to nothing.
+
+Split it into ZOOM_DEFAULT_ABS/REL/VEL, each placed after its pan/tilt
+counterpart, in the PTZConfiguration of GetProfile(s) (media and
+media2) and Get(Configuration|Configurations).
